From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Anthony Fu (via agent)" <reg-github-bot@antfu.me>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:17:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(server): keep searching when a project icon candidate is
 rejected

Project icon discovery stopped at the first file whose name matched, even
when it then failed the size or square check, so a valid icon next to it
was never found. Each candidate is now validated during the search, and
discovery also covers docs/, res/ and .github/, ranks logo above icon, and
accepts WebP and JPEG.

Squashed from upstream PR https://github.com/getpaseo/paseo/pull/8529
(ff44e1067, 526adb216).

On top of the PR: when no icon file is found and the project's origin is on
GitHub, the daemon uses the owner's avatar (github.com/<owner>.png, so
nuxt/devtools gets github.com/nuxt.png). A custom icon and any local icon
still win. Avatars are fetched with a 3 s timeout and cached per owner in
memory: a day for a found or missing owner, ten minutes after a failure.
Offline daemons keep the initial.

Fork-Change: F-1
